WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.520
It is
a privilege to be a detective.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.440
Mark Birch: You deal
with lots and lots of

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.280
horrible things,
that comes with the territory.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.920
The majority of us
don't have to see these things,

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.200
don't have to
deal with these things.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.760
The launch of the fifth
murder enquiry in such

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:20.920
a short space of time...

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.480
Martin Brunning: Justice
for the victims is absolutely

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.000
the most important thing.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.040
- You've been arrested
on suspicion of attempted

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.280
murder and murder.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.440
- Could be worse.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.800
Officer PTC: We can
only imagine the grief of

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.120
the families who lost
their loved ones in such brutal

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.440
circumstances.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.520
- ... with your DNA.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.520
How can that be?

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.240
- No comment.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.120
Journalist PTC: The judge
said the murder showed

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.280
a degree of
premeditation and planning.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.560
He'd been stabbed and beaten.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.920
Howard Groves: It was very
much a manhunt at that stage

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.120
of the investigation.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.080
He knew that the walls
were closing in on him.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:58.200
Stewart Gull: I always remember
a more experienced officer

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.960
telling me, you know, you,
you never forget these jobs,

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.440
and he was right.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.800
VO: These are the detectives
who solved some of Britain's

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.840
most notorious homicides.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.960
Now they re-live those cases.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.720
Martin Brunning: Every fear
that I had was being realised in

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:17.400
front of my eyes.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:21.160
VO: Through every twist and Turn of the investigation ...

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.880
Mark Birch: The only way you
forget about it is ...

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:24.840
is when you're asleep.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.760
VO: Their personal accounts
reveal what it really takes

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.960
to capture a killer
and bring them to justice.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.560
Howard Groves:
As a detective, you know,

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.600
there, there can't be any
greater honour than for you

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.760
to investigate the death- or
murder- of another human being.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.880
Martin PTC: This investigation has so many shocking elements

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.320
to it,
one after the other.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:08.640
And at no stage when this
investigation started did it

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.160
ever occur to me that
the person responsible for

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:14.840
so much damage was a woman.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.360
Martin PTC: What makes a
murder case different

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:27.800
from other cases?

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:33.400
The impact of your actions
will always be remembered

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:36.080
by the people
affected by that murder.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.640
And absolutely crucial
that it's the right memory.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.800
Until the person that we are
after is safely locked away

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:47.240
from society, I don't rest.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.520
And my team recognise the
importance of what we're doing

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:51.600
on behalf of the victim.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:03:00.680
The person with no
Voice, we're doing it for them.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.360
Martin PTC: This
case started in Easter in,

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.560
er, twenty-thirteen,
the Bank Holiday weekend.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.200
I was working as the Major Crime
Senior Investigator covering

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:18.240
Bedfordshire, Cambridgeshire
and Hertfordshire.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:23.440
Martin PTC: Around
nine-sixteen a 999 call was

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.280
received by the
fire service in Cambridgeshire.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.640
A couple of guys had come
across a car fire in

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.800
the village of Yaxley.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.840
VO: Unknown to police,
that car fire at Yaxley

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:42.480
is connected to something
far more disturbing waiting

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.120
on the other
side of Peterborough.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:49.200
Martin PTC: I was
on the A1 between Huntingdon

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.920
and Peterborough and
the phone rang in the car

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.840
and it was one of the,
the DI's from Peterborough said

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:02.640
'Look, a body's turned up,
by a dog-walker, in a ditch'.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.680
VO: It was a villager
walking his dog who found

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.360
the body off a single
track road near Peterborough.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.960
Journalist PTC: The body was
found here after half past

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.600
ten on Saturday morning,
close to Newborough and the A16.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:19.560
Martin PTC: I was told that
visually the person looked like

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.760
the photo that we had as part
of a missing person enquiry.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:25.640
It felt like there was
going to be really bad

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:26.920
news on the end of this.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.520
Martin PTC:
I went straight to the scene.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:35.400
So I'm driving down this farm
track and I see the police

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:39.440
car ahead and I stop
my car close by and I decided

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:42.480
to walk through a field
and it was- I had a suit on-

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:45.880
it was muddy,
it was just difficult to get to,

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.680
and it was freezing cold.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.760
It was a really
cold Easter weekend.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:56.760
And eventually I, I found
a route in towards the body

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.760
and straight away was struck
by the position of, of the body.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:05.480
The first thing I thought
was that somebody was

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.720
humiliating this person.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:12.600
In all of my experience,
this stood out as 'fixed'.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:18.760
It had been framed, whoever did
this wanted people to see it.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:23.480
Martin PTC: The position
of this man was that he was

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:28.400
in a ditch and his buttocks
were pointing very clearly

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:29.760
up towards the sky.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:34.120
And, and it was, it felt
and looked very much like he,

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.920
he'd been put
in that position to degrade him.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.840
He was wearing a black sequinned
dress which was obviously a,

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:45.120
a woman's garment, um, but it'd
been pulled right up above

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:48.480
his waist and it,
it was just the strangest thing.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:55.000
Martin PTC: So I could see
blood on his arms and at that

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.960
stage I, I don't know
how this man has died so the,

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.040
the critical questions for me
are: What are we dealing with?

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:02.640
Is it a murder?

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:03.680
Is this misadventure?

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:06.200
And it was really, really
obvious when we turned him

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:11.560
over onto his
back that he'd been murdered.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.840
He'd been stabbed.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:16.920
Centrally located stab wounds.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:21.040
He'd got injuries on his
forearm and between his fingers.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:23.560
Defence wounds
where a hand had really,

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:26.080
had obviously
been put up to stop the force,

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:30.520
which said to me that this
is a really violent way to die.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:37.840
Martin PTC: I'm starting to
look around and I'm standing

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.880
in a field
for as far as the eye can see,

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.200
it felt like
it was the middle of nowhere.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:45.480
There's no cameras,
there's no witnesses,

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:48.520
this is a really
difficult terrain to start

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:51.920
a murder investigation.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.280
And I'm starting
to think Why a dress?

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:55.960
How did he die?

00:06:56.040 --> 00:07:00.600
What's it going
to take to unravel this job?

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:04.640
VO: Police quickly confirm
the identity of the victim in

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:08.680
the ditch as 48-year-old
missing local man Kevin Lee.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:13.720
VO: What police knew
of Kevin's life threw little

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:19.920
light on his violent death.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:24.080
Martin PTC: Kevin was to all
intents and purposes a family

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:27.360
man, he had a business in
Peterborough renting properties,

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:29.800
and had a lovely family.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.880
Had a lovely family.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:35.480
Kevin was, um,
a genuinely empathetic man.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:39.800
He would give accommodation
to people who had certain

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:42.440
vulnerabilities, and that
was certainly a trait in

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:43.720
a number of his tenants.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.640
He was showing a
huge amount of, um,

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:50.040
support for people that
just needed a leg-up in life.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:55.560
There was no logical explanation
at that point that I was stood

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:59.120
looking into that ditch
to explain or account

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.960
why Kevin was, was there
and in those circumstances.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:08.280
VO: Kevin's disappearance
had been reported by his wife

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:09.840
barely twelve hours earlier.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:13.440
Martin PTC: Kevin went
missing around six o'clock in

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:15.680
the evening on Good Friday.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.440
Er, should have been at home, didn't come back.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:22.280
Kevin's wife was
clearly concerned,

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:24.880
it's completely
out of character for him.

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:28.400
And she kind of started
her own police investigation,

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.600
for want of a better term.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:35.000
She identified from his online
mobile phone account people

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:38.160
that he'd been in contact with, or numbers that had

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.280
contacted his phone,
and she just randomly started

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:43.520
calling people as any...

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:47.360
Fearful wife perhaps would do.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:52.760
She never particularly knew who
she was speaking to but would,

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.680
would ask the
questions, 'Have you seen Kevin,

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:55.880
he's not come home?'

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:59.160
And around
quarter past nine she makes, er,

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:02.320
one of a number of telephone
calls and the call connected

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:05.600
for two seconds
before the call was dropped.

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:08.920
That phone
call was absolutely crucial.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:13.120
That two seconds
of telecommunications data

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:17.760
was enough to identify
the location of the phone,

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:20.720
and it was within
the precise location of

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:25.280
the car fire in Yaxley.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:29.320
VO: That burnt-out
car belonged to Kevin Lee.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:34.120
The mobile phone, almost
certainly, to his murderer.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.640
Martin PTC: Kevin's wife,
she didn't know it but

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.360
she was talking to the
person that killed her husband.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:46.000
This is a
real breakthrough moment.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:49.360
If we can unpick
who owns that telephone,

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.000
we've got the key
to this investigation,

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:51.920
as to who killed Kevin.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:58.200
VO: Using cell site analysis,
police quickly

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.840
have their answer.

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:05.280
Martin PTC: That phone
belonged to Joanne Dennehy.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.440
Looking at the circumstances,
there's Kevin in the ditch,

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:14.000
in a dress, a really violent
attack with a knife ...

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:16.600
I never assumed that
this was the work of a woman.

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:20.880
We researched Joanne Dennehy.

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:24.360
She was a,
a local to Peterborough.

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:27.320
She's a relatively
low-level criminal.

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:32.680
She was troubled in adulthood,
um, and was fairly anti-social.

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:37.920
VO: Joanne is also the
mother of two children who

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.600
live elsewhere
with their father.

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:42.880
Martin PTC: We make some
enquiries and after speaking

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:47.040
to Kevin's business partner
it was very clearly obvious

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:54.560
that Joanne knew Kevin as
a landlord and business owner.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:58.400
VO: Police now have a
prime suspect and a location

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:02.120
to investigate - the bedsit
that Joanne rents from Kevin.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:04.520
Martin PTC: We go into
her house, we get a warrant,

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:09.240
we're going in, we're
going to see what we can find.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:13.800
VO: The police don't
find Joanne at the property.

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.640
But they
do make a sinister discovery.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.720
Martin PTC: In the garden
of this property is

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:22.240
a single mattress
which is soaked in blood.

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:30.120
VO: Detective
Martin Brunning: has a vicious

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:33.880
murder case on his hands
and a prime suspect at large.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.080
The hunt is on to find her.

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:40.680
Martin PTC: I was content at
that point that Joanne

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:43.480
Dennehy was a suspect
in the murder of Kevin Lee,

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:46.760
and all the energy over that
weekend was to get our hands

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:48.720
on her as quickly as possible.

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:52.120
Martin PTC: There's a, a
heavily bloodstained mattress

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:55.560
in a house
in Byfield where Joanne lived,

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:59.160
and I'm thinking 'Is
this where Kevin was killed?'

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:02.120
But I'm also being told that
one of the tenants is missing.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:06.360
Martin PTC: A guy called
John Chapman who was vulnerable,

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:10.120
should have
been there, wasn't.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:13.400
This man who I'm told leads
this simple lifestyle

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:16.320
of drinking and sleeping
and never venturing too far

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:17.800
from the house is not there.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.040
Where is he?

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:21.360
So is it a missing guy
or is it something terrible's

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.120
happened to him?

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:24.600
And I'm thinking if it's
something terrible's happened

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:27.560
to him, and
we've actually got two murders,

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:29.520
then how much of a risk is
she to the public that

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.640
she's not going to stop?

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:35.240
VO: Acutely
aware of the public risk,

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:37.800
detective Brunning
widens the net.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:43.520
Martin PTC: I put her picture
in the media over that weekend.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:46.760
We know she's distinctive, she's
got this tattoo on her face,

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:50.440
and I'm thinking we're going to
get a line of enquiry from this.

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:51.760
We're going to
get a breakthrough,

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:54.160
somebody's going to say
'I've just seen Joanne Dennehy,

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:56.880
I've seen why you want her,'
and I'm thinking we're going

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.720
to get control around
this really, really quickly.

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:02.840
VO: It soon becomes apparent
that wherever Joanne is,

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.440
she's not alone.

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:07.880
Martin PTC: We identify
that there's a very strong

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:12.240
correlation between her mobile
phone activity and that of an

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:13.920
associate called Gary Stretch.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:19.800
Martin PTC: Over that
weekend it is clear that Joanne

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:21.360
was evading the police.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:24.000
We could see from her,
the movement of her telephone

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:26.320
that she was turning
it on, she was turning it off.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:29.760
She, she clearly needed to use
it from time to time and it was

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:33.360
obvious from Gary's phone that
he was turning it on and off.

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:37.400
And when we overlaid the imagery
of where that was happening it

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:40.200
was as clear as day that those
two were in company together,

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:43.000
on the run, knew
they were wanted by the police,

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:45.400
and were doing all they
could to avoid being captured.

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:49.240
VO: Joanne and Gary had done
odd jobs together for Kevin Lee,

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:53.120
including collecting rent and
dealing with difficult tenants.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:57.280
Martin PTC: Gary is a
career criminal in Peterborough.

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:00.720
He's been dubbed, er, 'Britain's
Tallest Burglar'- a giant of a

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:02.720
man at seven-foot-three.

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:06.120
If these two are
together, even more distinctive,

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.360
even more reason
to put them into the media.

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:10.360
The public are go
... going to see these two,

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:14.200
er, together and
think 'Actually, I've seen that,

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.200
I've seen that on the news'.

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:18.360
So I was really excited about
that and hoped that that

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:21.040
would give us the opportunity
to, to get them arrested really,

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:21.680
really quickly.

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:24.400
VO: Now the police have
released pictures of two people

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:27.200
they want to question in
connection with the stabbing-

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:30.480
Gary Stretch
who is 47 and seven-foot-three,

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:36.120
and Joanne Dennehy who is 30
with a distinctive green tattoo.

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:45.120
Police urge anyone with
any information to come forward.

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:46.560
Martin PTC:
And we get nothing.

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:49.240
For the whole weekend-
it's Easter,

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:52.240
people are with their families,
they're not looking at the news,

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:53.560
they're not interested.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:58.280
This woman is roaming
around the east of England,

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:00.800
I don't know where she is,
I don't know what she's doing,

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:03.840
but what I do know is that
the public are at risk if

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:05.040
she's not in custody.

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:14.640
Martin PTC: I was in the
canteen at Police Headquarters,

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:18.640
I'd just bought a cup of coffee
and I was talking to a colleague

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:20.560
about 'stuff', the job that we
were investigating and I'd got

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:25.960
the information to say 'Oh,
we've just taken a phone call

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.240
from a, a Norfolk bobby who's
got a registration number of the

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.920
car, and thinks it's Dennehy'.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:31.840
And I said
'Oh, thanks very much'.

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:35.560
And I carried on the
conversation and it wasn't until

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:38.480
about a minute in I thought
... 'We've got the registration

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:39.160
number of the car'.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:41.480
It was like this
moment of realisation.

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:45.840
I was so engrossed in the
conversation that I kinda turned

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:49.640
on my heels and flew across to
the Major Incident Room

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:53.360
and said 'Right, let's get this
registration number into ANPR,

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:55.000
Automatic Number
Plate Recognition,

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:59.000
I want to know
where it is, Iet's track it'.

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:02.240
VO: A minor theft eighty
miles away had given a clue

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:04.400
to Joanne's
possible whereabouts.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.760
Martin PTC: A detective in
Norfolk - he was investigating

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:12.120
a shoplifting where a car had
driven onto the forecourt

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.720
of a petrol
station just outside of Cromer,

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:18.000
and had recognised the
similarity of a female who'd

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.560
got out of the passenger seat
and went into the, the store,

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:25.240
stole a whole load of
groceries and food and then

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:28.200
got back in the car.

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:30.160
Martin PTC: And that was
the absolute breakthrough

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:33.400
in order to, to, to
start to track Joanne and Gary.

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:37.080
We were able to start
honing down really where

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:39.120
that vehicle was.

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:41.120
We recognised that
it was a green Vauxhall Astra,

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:47.240
that it had been activating ANPR
all around the east of England,

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:50.000
that in fact at one
stage we were getting live

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:53.960
time notifications that
the car was travelling on

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:58.200
the M5 south-west towards
the West Mercia police area.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:03.320
VO: A local murder hunt
has now become a three-county

00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:04.320
investigation.

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:06.680
Martin PTC: We were straight on
the phone to West Mercia

00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:10.720
saying 'Look, this
car has got these people in it,

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:13.120
they've certainly killed
one person in Cambridgeshire,

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:16.000
you need to get your hands
on them and please ring me

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:16.680
when you've done it'.

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:19.040
And it was as,
as fast-moving as that.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:21.520
It was exhilarating,
it was pressured,

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:25.000
it was we're nearing the end,
we're going to get our hands

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.360
on these people and, and then
we can put our foot on

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:30.960
the ball and take
stock of exactly what's gone on.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:34.600
VO: As sightings come in,
Martin's team is able to piece

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:38.240
together an audacious picture
of Joanne and Gary's movements

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.840
over the Bank Holiday weekend.

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:43.680
The evidence shows Dennehy
and Stretch walking into

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:46.880
the services
on the M5, hand in hand,

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:48.800
without a care in the world.

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:50.480
Martin PTC: They were
breaking into people's houses,

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:53.480
stealing food, stealing
cameras to turn into cash

00:17:53.520 --> 00:17:54.520
whilst on the run.

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:59.080
Martin PTC: They were taking
pictures of themselves in

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:01.160
towns throughout
the east of England.

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:07.000
It was an elaborate
cops-and-robbers event that

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:10.480
they added and weaved
into an element of fun,

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:11.600
that it was thrilling,

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:14.520
it was exciting,
they were untouchable,

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:18.760
and this romantic relationship
that was blossoming whilst on

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:23.080
the run from the police has
so many parallels to Bonnie

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:26.600
and Clyde that
it, it's almost beyond belief.

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:31.480
VO: Martin and his team wait
nervously for news from West

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:32.520
Mercia Police.

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:35.720
Martin PTC: I'm literally
pacing up and down the, the,

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:39.160
the Major Incident Room waiting
for the phone call to say we've

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:40.640
got her, we've got him.

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:46.920
That sense of pheww, pressure's
off, and it doesn't come.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:49.240
And I'm getting
increasingly anxious.

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:51.880
What I anticipated
would happen is,

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:55.040
is that the cops in West Mercia
would come across the vehicle,

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:57.880
they would stop
it, they would lock them up,

00:18:57.960 --> 00:18:59.840
and we would get a phone call.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:02.120
How wrong was I.

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:10.200
Martin PTC: Eventually that
phone call comes but it comes

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:13.440
with the caveat that there's
been a whole load of carnage

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:16.200
in Hereford.

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:19.800
VO: Involved in that carnage,
two people matching Joanne

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.400
and Gary's descriptions.

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:24.680
Martin PTC: The information
that we were getting was that

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:27.400
Gary and, and Joanne were
together in Hereford in

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:32.120
the car and Joanne
had attacked two strangers.

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:35.240
Two men horrendously
with a knife within

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.360
a ten-minute timeframe.

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:40.800
Which realised every fear
that I had about just what

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:41.840
she was capable of doing.

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:45.600
VO: Those two men
were 64-year-old Robin Bereza,

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:52.520
attacked while walking his dog,
as was 56-year-old John Rogers.

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:55.040
John PTC:
She was stabbing in, my chest.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:58.400
She said,
um, 'Look, you're bleeding,

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:00.920
I'd better do some more'.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:05.600
And I think I said
'Just leave me alone please.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:09.880
Please leave me alone.' And then
when it did finally stop, um,

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:14.440
I just thought well this
is it, I'm, I'm going to die.

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:20.360
VO: John Rogers received
more than thirty stab wounds.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:25.200
Both he and Robin Bereza barely
survived the Unprovoked attacks.

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:28.080
Martin PTC: We've
got one murdered, one missing,

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:31.920
two fighting for their lives, so
it was a very kind of sobering

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:37.720
phone call
for a whole host of reasons.

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:40.080
Martin PTC:
Joanne was on a killing spree.

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:43.840
She had done
two, she wanted to do some more,

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:46.040
she had
those conversations with Gary,

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:49.280
it was very clear that until
the cops intervened

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:51.760
and stopped her
she was going to carry on.

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.800
VO: Joanne Dennehy
is wanted for murder in

00:20:57.840 --> 00:21:00.840
Peterborough and has been
seen stabbing two more

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:02.440
victims in Hereford.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:08.120
At ten past four on
Tuesday afternoon West Mercia

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:12.000
Police finally bring
her violent rampage to an end.

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:18.320
Martin PTC: We are
told that eventually, er,

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:20.760
Joanne and Gary have been
arrested, they're in custody,

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.960
the public were safe.

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:25.680
But it
came at a terrible cost in, er,

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:28.000
Robin Bereza and John
Rogers suffering such

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:31.200
terrible injuries.

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:33.600
VO: When Joanne is arrested
she shows little of

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:36.480
the blood lust that's
fuelled her brutal attacks.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:40.880
Martin PTC: Joanne was caught
in the vehicle which had

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:43.880
parked up after
the second stabbing.

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:48.520
She was a passenger in the front
seat, er, she was very calm.

00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:53.000
She engaged with the officers
and even produced the knife

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:56.800
that she had just used
on the two men in Hereford

00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:58.240
and handed it
over to the officers.

00:21:58.320 --> 00:22:01.400
VO: Joanne is brought
to Hereford Police Station

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:02.920
for booking.

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:03.680
- Afternoon.

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:07.240
- Afternoon.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:09.120
- And you are?

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:11.480
- Joanne Christina Dennehy.

00:22:11.560 --> 00:22:13.360
- So you've been arrested
on suspicion of attempted

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:19.080
murder and murder, ok?

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:23.880
Martin PTC: Joanne presented at
the custody desk as if she

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:27.240
was in a really euphoric
state and the video that I saw

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:31.840
subsequently showed her in
a really relaxed frame of mind.

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:34.440
- Would you be cheery
if you were up for attempted

00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:35.600
murder and murder?

00:22:35.640 --> 00:22:36.600
- I wouldn't but ...

00:22:36.680 --> 00:22:38.320
- No, but I'm still smiling.

00:22:38.400 --> 00:22:39.600
- I don't know
anything about it.

00:22:39.680 --> 00:22:42.640
I was just out
enjoying the sunshine.

00:22:42.680 --> 00:22:44.560
- You'll be reading about
it in the newspapers shortly.

00:22:44.640 --> 00:22:46.200
- Say again.

00:22:46.240 --> 00:22:48.480
- You'll be reading about
it in the newspapers shortly.

00:22:48.520 --> 00:22:50.520
- Well I'll look forward to it.

00:22:50.600 --> 00:22:52.160
- You're a decent copper.

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:54.040
I'm a crap killer, ain't I?

00:22:54.080 --> 00:22:56.240
- Well you've been caught so ...

00:22:56.320 --> 00:22:57.640
Martin PTC: She was joking
with the officers that were,

00:22:57.720 --> 00:22:59.520
er, escorting her.

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:02.600
Her humour was
really inappropriate.

00:23:02.680 --> 00:23:03.960
- It could be worse.

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:06.520
I could
be big, fat, black and ugly.

00:23:06.560 --> 00:23:07.560
- You could be what?

00:23:07.600 --> 00:23:09.000
- Big, fat, black and ugly.

00:23:09.040 --> 00:23:10.200
- Yeah you could be.

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:11.600
- So it could be worse.

00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:12.960
- I'm not sure
how that would be worse though.

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:14.840
- Yeah it would.

00:23:14.880 --> 00:23:15.640
- Would it?

00:23:15.680 --> 00:23:16.280
- Yeah.

00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:19.480
- You've got very
distinctive eyebrows.

00:23:19.560 --> 00:23:22.120
- I know, so you keep saying.

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:28.160
- Now everyone's
looking at your eyebrows.

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:30.400
- We've got some suitable
clothing for you to wear Joanne.

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:31.880
- A tracksuit and plimsolls?

00:23:31.920 --> 00:23:33.360
- Could well be.

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:34.800
- And a tracksuit top.

00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:36.800
- Ey it's better
than nothing innit?

00:23:36.880 --> 00:23:39.000
- Fucking glamorous that is.

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.040
Martin PTC:
Just strange, strange behaviour.

00:23:41.120 --> 00:23:43.920
It was as if she'd
partitioned it off and this

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:46.240
was all one big joke.

00:23:46.320 --> 00:23:49.600
And that she
was at the centre of this joke.

00:23:49.640 --> 00:23:51.680
- Right, so what am I up for?

00:23:51.760 --> 00:23:53.800
Attempted murder and murder?

00:23:53.840 --> 00:23:56.120
- You've been arrested
on suspicion of attempted

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:57.920
murder and murder.

00:23:58.000 --> 00:24:00.600
- Could be worse.

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:09.360
- Thanks.

00:24:09.440 --> 00:24:10.080
- You're welcome.

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:10.960
- That's lovely.

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:12.280
- Not bad for a murderer.

00:24:12.360 --> 00:24:14.800
- It's a
good one actually, yeah.

00:24:14.880 --> 00:24:15.880
Martin
PTC: All eyes were on her,

00:24:15.960 --> 00:24:18.040
you got a sense that she really
enjoyed it and was playing

00:24:18.120 --> 00:24:21.640
up to it as if it was a crowd
there for her entertainment.

00:24:21.680 --> 00:24:28.920
- No, it's nothing!

00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:30.360
- Right, come on then Joanne.

00:24:30.440 --> 00:24:32.680
- Can I have some food first?

00:24:32.720 --> 00:24:35.920
- I'll take your
order when you get in the cell.

00:24:35.960 --> 00:24:38.120
What do you want to drink?

00:24:38.200 --> 00:24:40.440
- I feel like
the incredible hulk.

00:24:40.520 --> 00:24:43.960
VO: Amongst the jokes, Joanne
makes a chilling revelation.

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:46.520
Martin PTC: She told
the custody officer at the time,

00:24:46.560 --> 00:24:51.440
in a kind of prancing around
the, the custody room style,

00:24:51.520 --> 00:24:53.280
that she'd killed five people.

00:24:53.360 --> 00:24:59.640
Did she mean in her calculation
that the five people that

00:24:59.720 --> 00:25:03.480
she'd killed included
John Rogers and Robin Bereza?

00:25:03.560 --> 00:25:04.800
Have we got more murders?

00:25:04.880 --> 00:25:07.880
Um, how, how does this kind
of progress, how does it unfold?

00:25:07.920 --> 00:25:10.840
We've got the complexity
of a murder in Cambridgeshire,

00:25:10.920 --> 00:25:14.360
we've got two people that are,
sound like they're going to die

00:25:14.440 --> 00:25:18.680
in Hereford, and actually
it's a really pressurised time.

00:25:18.760 --> 00:25:20.720
Really pressured.

00:25:28.080 --> 00:25:32.160
Martin PTC: So Tuesday we
all go home knowing that

00:25:32.240 --> 00:25:33.440
Joanne is in custody.

00:25:33.480 --> 00:25:36.720
We all felt slightly more
at ease by the fact that we

00:25:36.800 --> 00:25:38.120
knew she was locked away.

00:25:38.200 --> 00:25:43.120
We planned to reconvene
on the Wednesday, take stock,

00:25:43.200 --> 00:25:46.000
work out what was important
and really think about what

00:25:46.080 --> 00:25:49.160
we were going to do next.

00:25:58.560 --> 00:26:02.040
Martin PTC: On Wednesday I
came into work to start to join

00:26:02.120 --> 00:26:07.040
the, the investigation in West
Mercia with Cambridgeshire

00:26:07.080 --> 00:26:10.000
and as I was briefing the team
the phone on the desk next to me

00:26:10.080 --> 00:26:14.040
rang and I picked it up and
it was the force Control Room

00:26:14.080 --> 00:26:18.320
saying, er, we've had a report
that a body has been found

00:26:18.360 --> 00:26:20.800
in a ditch in Thorney Dyke.

00:26:20.880 --> 00:26:24.360
And instinctively I thought...

00:26:24.400 --> 00:26:27.160
that's going
to be John Chapman.

00:26:27.200 --> 00:26:29.400
We hadn't
explained his absence,

00:26:29.480 --> 00:26:32.640
he was so close
to Dennehy in lifestyle terms,

00:26:32.720 --> 00:26:35.840
living in the same house, this
is going to be John Chapman.

00:26:35.920 --> 00:26:38.800
Martin PTC: Before I'd had
a chance to do anything

00:26:38.840 --> 00:26:41.000
or make any
decision, the phone rang again.

00:26:41.040 --> 00:26:44.880
I'll never forget this phone
call for as long as I live.

00:26:44.960 --> 00:26:49.040
It said, 'Are you aware of
the body that has been found

00:26:49.120 --> 00:26:50.040
in Thorney Dyke?'

00:26:50.120 --> 00:26:53.520
And I said,
'Yes, I've just been briefed'.

00:26:53.600 --> 00:26:55.920
And the woman
in the Control Room said to me,

00:26:55.960 --> 00:26:58.520
'There's two bodies'.

00:26:58.560 --> 00:26:59.560
And it stunned me.

00:26:59.640 --> 00:27:04.400
And I held the
phone to my chest and just said,

00:27:04.480 --> 00:27:06.480
'There's two bodies'.

00:27:07.280 --> 00:27:09.640
And you could hear a pin drop.

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:18.440
And I had this - the only way
I can describe it is a rush of

00:27:18.480 --> 00:27:22.600
adrenaline of What is going on?

00:27:22.680 --> 00:27:24.120
What's happening?

00:27:24.200 --> 00:27:26.160
When's this going to stop?

00:27:26.240 --> 00:27:31.200
However bad it has been
up to this point with Kevin,

00:27:31.280 --> 00:27:36.120
Robin Bereza, John Rogers,
however bad that has been for

00:27:36.200 --> 00:27:38.680
those people and those families,
this has just got

00:27:38.760 --> 00:27:40.440
a whole lot worse.

00:27:40.520 --> 00:27:42.680
That phone call
absolutely changed the game.

00:27:42.760 --> 00:27:46.520
And I realised that if this was
the work of Joanne Dennehy

00:27:46.600 --> 00:27:47.880
we're dealing
with a serial killer.

00:27:47.920 --> 00:27:52.920
Martin PTC: So I went
down to Thorney Dyke

00:28:00.800 --> 00:28:04.360
and saw a remarkably
similar landscape to Newborough,

00:28:04.400 --> 00:28:06.360
where Kevin's body was dumped.

00:28:06.440 --> 00:28:11.800
A ditch alongside a field with
very little human habitation,

00:28:11.840 --> 00:28:15.160
and quite a shocking scene
actually of two bodies side

00:28:15.240 --> 00:28:18.120
by side, no more
than a few inches between them.

00:28:18.200 --> 00:28:24.560
VO: For Detective Brunning
there's a sickening feeling

00:28:24.640 --> 00:28:25.560
of déjà vu.

00:28:25.640 --> 00:28:27.920
Martin PTC: It was
obvious that there was a huge,

00:28:27.960 --> 00:28:31.520
huge similarity with the
circumstances of Kevin's death,

00:28:31.560 --> 00:28:35.960
in that there were stab
wounds in the chest of both men,

00:28:36.040 --> 00:28:40.040
localised to the
heart area, and in some numbers.

00:28:40.120 --> 00:28:45.680
And again, indicative
of really ferocious attack.

00:28:45.760 --> 00:28:51.240
I ... I've been in to countless
murder scenes but I wouldn't be

00:28:51.320 --> 00:28:54.440
a human being with a beating
heart in my body if I didn't

00:28:54.520 --> 00:28:56.200
look at that,
and look down in this case,

00:28:56.280 --> 00:29:00.960
at those two bodies and think
... it's two more families that

00:29:01.040 --> 00:29:02.320
I've got to
send officers to, er,

00:29:02.360 --> 00:29:07.520
and tell them the news that
their loved ones are killed.

00:29:07.600 --> 00:29:10.280
VO: One of the bodies in the
ditch closely resembles

00:29:10.360 --> 00:29:11.920
Joanne's former housemate.

00:29:11.960 --> 00:29:17.720
Martin PTC: One looked
distinctly like John Chapman.

00:29:17.800 --> 00:29:21.360
Next to him was the body of, of
a complete stranger - stranger

00:29:21.440 --> 00:29:26.000
to the investigation - and
I distinctly remember looking at

00:29:26.040 --> 00:29:31.320
those two bodies and thinking Mr
Unknown - as he was at the time

00:29:31.400 --> 00:29:34.480
- has been there
much, much longer than John has.

00:29:34.520 --> 00:29:37.520
What does this mean for the
timeline of this investigation?

00:29:37.600 --> 00:29:41.720
And for me it meant
that Joanne's killing spree had

00:29:41.760 --> 00:29:42.960
started much earlier.

00:29:43.040 --> 00:29:47.520
VO: Martin and his team now
have two injured, three dead,

00:29:47.560 --> 00:29:50.760
and no idea
what the final tally might be.

00:29:50.800 --> 00:29:53.760
Martin PTC: How many more
phone calls are we going to

00:29:53.800 --> 00:29:57.160
get to say bodies
have been dumped in ditches?

00:29:57.240 --> 00:29:59.920
How many more
people has she killed?

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:04.240
When the hell
is this going to stop?

00:30:11.720 --> 00:30:13.280
Martin PTC: The prime line
of enquiry now was to confirm

00:30:13.320 --> 00:30:15.520
the identity
of who I thought was John.

00:30:15.560 --> 00:30:21.040
Er, we very quickly did that
... and we needed to identify

00:30:21.120 --> 00:30:24.960
this unknown man.

00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:27.120
Martin PTC: We got mobile
fingerprint scan technology down

00:30:27.200 --> 00:30:31.040
to the scene and very quickly
identified that the man next

00:30:31.120 --> 00:30:33.240
to John was
Lukasz Slaboszewski.

00:30:33.320 --> 00:30:38.320
Thirty-one-year-old Lukasz
had settled in Peterborough

00:30:38.400 --> 00:30:40.680
from Poland
eight years earlier.

00:30:40.760 --> 00:30:43.320
Martin PTC: We
knew very little about Lukasz,

00:30:43.400 --> 00:30:45.520
he lived a
fairly simple lifestyle.

00:30:45.560 --> 00:30:50.960
It was absolutely crucial to
understand when Joanne Dennehy

00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:52.480
started the killing spree.

00:30:52.560 --> 00:30:56.000
Lukasz Slaboszewski
was a complete wild card

00:30:56.080 --> 00:30:57.760
to this investigation.

00:30:57.800 --> 00:31:01.160
What is the relevance
of Lukasz meeting his death

00:31:01.200 --> 00:31:03.320
at the hands of Joanne
Dennehy and being in that ditch?

00:31:03.400 --> 00:31:07.720
Perhaps that would then
lead on to why Kevin died

00:31:07.800 --> 00:31:09.160
and why John
Chapman died.

00:31:09.240 --> 00:31:12.880
VO: Forensic attention
turns back to the house

00:31:12.920 --> 00:31:15.640
where Joanne
and John Chapman had bedsits.

00:31:15.720 --> 00:31:18.480
Martin PTC: That heavily
bloodstained mattress in a house

00:31:18.520 --> 00:31:22.560
in Byfield where Joanne lived,
we get the DNA profile

00:31:22.640 --> 00:31:25.840
of the blood
from that mattress.

00:31:25.920 --> 00:31:27.160
This is John Chapman's blood.

00:31:27.200 --> 00:31:31.400
VO: The evidence Martin's
team has gathered pointing

00:31:31.440 --> 00:31:36.440
to Joanne Dennehy as
a serial killer is stacking up.

00:31:38.440 --> 00:31:40.960
Police have the body
and a bloody crime scene

00:31:41.040 --> 00:31:41.960
for John Chapman.

00:31:42.040 --> 00:31:44.880
VO: Now the focus of
the investigation turns

00:31:44.960 --> 00:31:46.080
to Lukasz Slaboszewski.

00:31:46.120 --> 00:31:49.120
Martin PTC: As you can imagine
and - and the investigation's

00:31:49.200 --> 00:31:51.680
huge now - um, and a number
of people that we were

00:31:51.720 --> 00:31:55.880
speaking to as
witnesses was in triple figures.

00:31:55.960 --> 00:32:00.560
And one person that we
spoke to told us that

00:32:00.640 --> 00:32:05.640
she had met Joanne at
a time before Kevin was killed,

00:32:07.720 --> 00:32:13.360
and she had been shown a
decomposing body of a man

00:32:13.440 --> 00:32:17.360
dumped in a wheelie
bin in the Peterborough area.

00:32:17.440 --> 00:32:19.320
Yes, of course we would have
wanted to know about that but

00:32:19.400 --> 00:32:21.800
the reality was,
given their age,

00:32:21.880 --> 00:32:25.640
I don't bear
any grudge to that individual.

00:32:25.720 --> 00:32:29.560
But Joanne chose
to traumatise her.

00:32:29.640 --> 00:32:33.120
VO: This new information
leads police to another

00:32:33.160 --> 00:32:35.840
of Kevin Lee's
properties at Rolleston Garth.

00:32:35.920 --> 00:32:39.400
Martin PTC: The forensic
picture is you can see two clear

00:32:39.440 --> 00:32:40.200
murder scenes.

00:32:40.240 --> 00:32:46.640
There were two killings
at that property, days apart,

00:32:46.680 --> 00:32:49.600
evidence that
Lukasz Slaboszewski was stabbed

00:32:49.680 --> 00:32:53.920
repeatedly in
the property and bled profusely.

00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:56.640
And there was a significant
amount of evidence to show that

00:32:56.720 --> 00:32:58.880
Kevin Lee subsequently
died in that property,

00:32:58.920 --> 00:33:01.000
with blood
distributed around the house.

00:33:01.080 --> 00:33:04.440
A clean-up
operation was clearly visible.

00:33:04.520 --> 00:33:07.760
We could show that Dennehy
and Stretch were in that

00:33:07.840 --> 00:33:10.200
crime scene at the
time it was being cleaned up,

00:33:10.280 --> 00:33:14.440
which linked them perfectly
to the totality of their

00:33:14.520 --> 00:33:17.400
Involvement
in this investigation.

00:33:17.440 --> 00:33:20.880
Gary does the disposing
of the bodies and the driving,

00:33:20.960 --> 00:33:23.280
and the cleaning up.

00:33:23.360 --> 00:33:24.600
Dennehy does the killing.

00:33:24.680 --> 00:33:28.880
That's the arrangement, that was
the Bonnie and Clyde image that

00:33:28.920 --> 00:33:33.920
the two of them wanted to
portray on their killing sprees.

00:33:37.800 --> 00:33:40.040
Martin PTC:
This case is surreal.

00:33:40.120 --> 00:33:44.640
If you sat in a pub with
one of your friends and tried

00:33:44.720 --> 00:33:48.080
to recreate
a story that a woman would,

00:33:48.160 --> 00:33:51.320
would go around the streets
of Peterborough killing men

00:33:51.400 --> 00:33:56.680
for fun, times three,
going on the run...

00:33:56.760 --> 00:34:00.880
savagely attacking two
men at random and then

00:34:00.960 --> 00:34:03.720
laugh at the world
after so much damage...

00:34:03.760 --> 00:34:06.720
all this was
being played out in real life.

00:34:08.480 --> 00:34:10.080
VO: Detective Martin
Brunning: is dealing with

00:34:10.160 --> 00:34:13.080
the rarest
of serial killers - a woman.

00:34:13.160 --> 00:34:16.720
One whose killings display an
extraordinary control

00:34:16.800 --> 00:34:19.440
over her victims.

00:34:19.520 --> 00:34:21.400
Martin PTC: Joanne Dennehy
in her own right is quite

00:34:21.440 --> 00:34:25.920
slight but somehow she managed
to overpower three men in such

00:34:26.000 --> 00:34:28.840
a way as to be able to deliver
such catastrophic injuries.

00:34:28.880 --> 00:34:32.720
Martin PTC: In all three cases
what was really interesting

00:34:32.800 --> 00:34:36.760
about the nature of the injuries
was ... there had to be

00:34:36.840 --> 00:34:40.080
an element of her
controlling the circumstances.

00:34:40.120 --> 00:34:43.960
It wasn't random, it wasn't
Robin Bereza and John Rogers

00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:48.080
in Hereford,
the frenzied set-upon mentality.

00:34:48.160 --> 00:34:51.080
These were localised
to the centre of the chest,

00:34:51.160 --> 00:34:53.360
around the heart.

00:34:53.400 --> 00:34:55.320
She had the capability
and the capacity to

00:34:55.400 --> 00:34:57.040
do that unchallenged.

00:34:57.080 --> 00:35:00.480
And we started to establish a
greater understanding of

00:35:00.560 --> 00:35:07.280
Joanne and her ... ability
to manipulate, to instil fear,

00:35:07.320 --> 00:35:09.920
to use emotion
to control other people.

00:35:09.960 --> 00:35:14.680
VO: For Joanne, emotional
seduction provided opportunity.

00:35:14.720 --> 00:35:19.160
Martin PTC: In
Kevin's case, and Lukasz's case,

00:35:19.200 --> 00:35:22.000
there was probably an emotional
dimension to the relationship

00:35:22.080 --> 00:35:25.960
and she would have exploited
that to get herself physically

00:35:26.000 --> 00:35:28.520
in a position to be able to
inflict the level and nature

00:35:28.600 --> 00:35:30.000
of ferocity that she did.

00:35:30.040 --> 00:35:36.680
VO: A few days after her
arrest by West Mercia police,

00:35:36.720 --> 00:35:39.160
Joanne is released
to the Cambridgeshire force

00:35:39.240 --> 00:35:43.840
for interrogation.

00:35:44.800 --> 00:35:48.920
POLICE OFFICER: Did
you murder Lukasz Slaboszewski?

00:35:48.960 --> 00:35:50.440
JOANNE DENNEHY: No comment.

00:35:50.520 --> 00:35:52.280
POLICE OFFICER:
Did you murder John Chapman?

00:35:52.360 --> 00:35:55.360
JOANNE DENNEHY: No comment.

00:35:55.400 --> 00:35:57.600
POLICE OFFICER:
Did you murder Kevin Lee?

00:35:57.640 --> 00:36:02.040
JOANNE DENNEHY: No comment.

00:36:02.560 --> 00:36:05.000
Martin PTC: We interviewed
Joanne at length but there

00:36:05.040 --> 00:36:07.360
were no answers.

00:36:07.440 --> 00:36:11.160
VO: In preparation
for the pre-trial hearing,

00:36:11.240 --> 00:36:16.440
Dennehy is subjected to
a full psychiatric examination.

00:36:24.360 --> 00:36:27.560
VO: But Joanne refuses the
opportunity for any disorders to

00:36:27.600 --> 00:36:31.360
be taken into consideration,
wanting full ownership of her

00:36:31.400 --> 00:36:35.080
crimes and recognition
as a notorious serial killer.

00:36:35.160 --> 00:36:40.040
Martin PTC: She has controlled
how she behaves at every

00:36:40.120 --> 00:36:41.840
juncture on every level.

00:36:41.880 --> 00:36:45.720
She behaved in a way that
she wanted the public to see.

00:36:45.800 --> 00:36:47.760
That's the person that
Joanne is, she calls the shots.

00:37:00.480 --> 00:37:04.640
VO: At Joanne's hearing
she has one last hand to play.

00:37:04.720 --> 00:37:06.960
Martin PTC: I was sat
in the Old Bailey in a packed

00:37:07.000 --> 00:37:10.600
courtroom, and crucially with
many family members there from,

00:37:10.640 --> 00:37:11.880
from the victims of this.

00:37:11.960 --> 00:37:14.720
All of the
evidence was going to be tested,

00:37:14.800 --> 00:37:18.040
everything
that we'd done held to proof,

00:37:18.080 --> 00:37:21.240
and for this to become a very
long complicated trial at some

00:37:21.280 --> 00:37:22.400
point in the future.

00:37:22.480 --> 00:37:26.600
VO: The time comes for
Dennehy to answer to

00:37:26.680 --> 00:37:28.360
the three charges of murder.

00:37:28.440 --> 00:37:33.440
Martin PTC: The clerk stood up
and read out the indictments to

00:37:37.120 --> 00:37:42.680
formally invite Dennehy
to plead Guilty or Not Guilty.

00:37:42.760 --> 00:37:47.120
And in, in anybody's estimation
and, and my own included,

00:37:47.200 --> 00:37:50.600
I did not for one second
anticipate that the plea was

00:37:50.680 --> 00:37:52.280
going to be
anything other than Not Guilty.

00:37:52.360 --> 00:37:56.640
On the first indictment
read she pleaded Guilty,

00:37:56.720 --> 00:37:58.720
to everybody's astonishment.

00:38:00.840 --> 00:38:06.680
And I recall being sat directly
behind her Counsel and his

00:38:06.760 --> 00:38:09.120
reaction was
one of absolute bewilderment.

00:38:09.200 --> 00:38:13.000
He looked at her as
much as to say 'What you doing?

00:38:13.080 --> 00:38:14.320
This wasn't what we agreed.

00:38:14.400 --> 00:38:16.800
This isn't the
instruction that you gave me'.

00:38:16.840 --> 00:38:19.520
And the second indictment was
read and she pleaded Guilty to

00:38:19.600 --> 00:38:21.600
that, and the third
indictment was read

00:38:21.640 --> 00:38:23.480
and she pleaded Guilty to that.

00:38:23.560 --> 00:38:25.200
Nobody expected
what was happening.

00:38:25.280 --> 00:38:28.520
It was an absolute farce.

00:38:28.600 --> 00:38:34.600
But when I reflect on it now,
it was Dennehy's finest moment.

00:38:34.680 --> 00:38:40.960
She had the whole
court room under her spell,

00:38:41.040 --> 00:38:43.200
she had everybody
looking at her,

00:38:43.240 --> 00:38:47.360
and she knew in process terms
this was the last chance

00:38:47.400 --> 00:38:50.440
for her to have
control over what was happening.

00:38:50.480 --> 00:38:54.240
VO: Joanne's pleas
have one welcome consequence.

00:38:54.280 --> 00:38:56.880
Martin PTC: Dennehy made
it absolutely clear that she was

00:38:56.920 --> 00:38:59.040
pleading Guilty to all of this.

00:38:59.080 --> 00:39:02.440
And I really...
will never forget actually

00:39:02.520 --> 00:39:04.400
a sense of relief.

00:39:04.480 --> 00:39:07.400
Not because of the fact
that she'd admitted what she had

00:39:07.480 --> 00:39:13.480
done, but actually the families
weren't going to have to sit

00:39:13.560 --> 00:39:18.800
and listen to all of the gore
and the horror of her behaviour.

00:39:18.840 --> 00:39:22.360
And I, and I
fe ... I felt so relieved that,

00:39:22.440 --> 00:39:26.640
that they weren't going
to have to be put through that.

00:39:29.280 --> 00:39:31.880
VO: Someone who once
knew Joanne well is her former

00:39:31.960 --> 00:39:35.600
partner, her children's father.

00:39:35.680 --> 00:39:38.680
I weren't too surprised if
I'm honest because of the way,

00:39:38.720 --> 00:39:40.720
how aggressive she was.

00:39:40.800 --> 00:39:43.160
But to murder three people?

00:39:43.200 --> 00:39:45.880
I think I've
had a lucky escape.

00:39:45.960 --> 00:39:50.880
I've been emotionally battered,
she just drained every bit that

00:39:50.960 --> 00:39:55.280
I had, she was happiest when
she was doing the wrong thing.

00:39:55.360 --> 00:39:58.240
I don't know, even today
I still, I feel cold about it.

00:39:58.280 --> 00:40:01.640
I was with that woman, I've got
two kids with her but...

00:40:01.680 --> 00:40:03.880
why would you
do that to your kids?

00:40:03.960 --> 00:40:05.240
And why would you
put them through that?

00:40:05.280 --> 00:40:10.320
VO: Three months later
Joanne Dennehy returns to

00:40:19.360 --> 00:40:22.800
the Old Bailey to be sentenced
by Mr. Justice Spencer.

00:40:22.840 --> 00:40:24.720
Matt Teale (newsreader):
The serial killer Joanne Dennehy

00:40:24.800 --> 00:40:27.600
will spend the rest of her life
in prison after killing three

00:40:27.680 --> 00:40:29.880
men and attempting
to kill two others in Hereford.

00:40:29.960 --> 00:40:32.160
Martin PTC: Dennehy
was sentenced to a whole-life

00:40:32.240 --> 00:40:34.640
tariff, which means
she'll never come out

00:40:34.720 --> 00:40:36.960
and that's absolutely right.

00:40:37.040 --> 00:40:39.760
And that's really important for
the families that she'll

00:40:39.840 --> 00:40:43.160
never be allowed
out to hurt other people.

00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:46.600
I remember walking out
of the Old Bailey that day

00:40:46.680 --> 00:40:50.480
and thinking I did
what I set out to achieve.

00:40:50.560 --> 00:40:54.160
And that is really important.

00:40:54.240 --> 00:40:57.680
For me, the best possible
outcome for a murder case is

00:40:57.760 --> 00:40:59.880
that justice is delivered.

00:40:59.960 --> 00:41:03.400
We can't bring the people
back but we can help families

00:41:03.440 --> 00:41:04.920
to move on.

00:41:10.520 --> 00:41:13.240
Martin PTC: There's a,
a really important photograph

00:41:13.280 --> 00:41:16.120
of Joanne as a,
as a really young girl in a blue

00:41:16.160 --> 00:41:20.000
chequered school uniform that came into the investigation.

00:41:20.080 --> 00:41:24.080
We were all looking at
that photograph saying

00:41:24.160 --> 00:41:25.160
we've got kids.

00:41:25.200 --> 00:41:29.800
I've got a daughter, and her
family would have looked at that

00:41:29.880 --> 00:41:32.960
as her school photo at some
point in the past as a young

00:41:33.000 --> 00:41:35.280
girl and thought
what a lovely little girl.

00:41:35.360 --> 00:41:39.160
Full of promise,
full of hope, full of future.

00:41:39.240 --> 00:41:43.720
But somewhere
along the line she turned bad.

00:41:43.800 --> 00:41:48.360
And I guess we all privately
think when is that tipping

00:41:48.440 --> 00:41:52.960
point, when that youngster in
that school uniform became the

00:41:53.040 --> 00:41:54.360
monster that is Joanne Dennehy?

00:41:54.440 --> 00:41:59.560
VO: There's one part
of the puzzle Martin has been

00:41:59.600 --> 00:42:00.520
unable to solve.

00:42:00.560 --> 00:42:03.560
Martin PTC: One
of the real frustrations, er,

00:42:03.600 --> 00:42:08.360
and probably the biggest
unanswered question - through

00:42:08.400 --> 00:42:11.520
all of this - is Why?

00:42:11.600 --> 00:42:13.480
To be able
to say to all of those families,

00:42:13.560 --> 00:42:15.480
'This is why
your loved one died'.

00:42:15.520 --> 00:42:20.120
We've never, ever had
the privilege of Joanne Dennehy

00:42:20.200 --> 00:42:23.880
having
the decency to tell us that.

00:42:23.920 --> 00:42:27.840
And I suspect that
will remain the case forever.

00:42:27.920 --> 00:42:32.760
VO: Joanne Dennehy's case
is one Detective Brunning

00:42:32.840 --> 00:42:33.760
will never forget.

00:42:33.800 --> 00:42:36.600
Martin PTC: Investigations
like this leave their mark,

00:42:36.680 --> 00:42:38.560
and they leave their mark
on everybody that comes

00:42:38.600 --> 00:42:40.520
into contact with it.

00:42:40.600 --> 00:42:44.120
The twists, the turns,
the way it shocked,

00:42:44.200 --> 00:42:47.760
the way it felt
out of control at times,

00:42:47.840 --> 00:42:50.920
the level of damage that she's
done to families fundamentally

00:42:51.000 --> 00:42:52.120
changes you as a person.

00:42:52.200 --> 00:42:57.160
It's always your loved ones that
don't see you for days on end.

00:42:57.240 --> 00:43:01.240
The personal cost at
the time is great but absolutely

00:43:01.320 --> 00:43:03.520
driven to do the very
best you can for those

00:43:03.560 --> 00:43:05.080
people that are
so deeply affected.

